preConditionHook:
// THE SESSION'S OWN MIDPOINT AS THE TARGET. On a trading-range day a reversal
// from near the day's extreme is expected to test the middle of the session's
// range so far, so the countertrend long is taken off there.
//
// THE RANGE IS THE SESSION SO FAR THROUGH THE PREVIOUS BAR, not through this
// one. Updating the running extremes first and afterwards testing this bar's high
// against the midpoint of a range this bar just widened would fire on EVERY bar
// that makes a new session extreme, since the new extreme is above its own
// midpoint by construction. priorHigh / priorLow hold the range as of the
// previous bar -- the same "ending one bar ago" convention RangeMidpointTarget
// uses on its fixed window.
//
// midpointFraction generalises the level from the low upward for a long and from
// the high downward for a short; at 0.5 both sides are the midpoint, which is
// Brooks's statement. minSessionBars is the second guard: with two or three bars
// printed the "midpoint of the session" is the middle of one or two bars and the
// target sits inside the current bar. It also covers the session's first bar,
// where priorHigh and priorLow still hold yesterday's numbers.
//
// Not RangeMidpointZone or RangeMidpointTarget, which band or target the
// midpoint of a FIXED N-bar window, and not CloseNearSessionRangeMidpoint, an
// Entry filter asking whether the close sits inside a band around the midpoint:
// this asks whether the bar's high REACHED the level, in the exit pane.
//
// SESSION MODEL per the standing decision: EL's date > date[1] mirrored as
// day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)), running extremes and a
// bars-into-session counter in locals reset there. Intraday bars only.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    barsIn = 1;
    sessHigh = high[0];
    sessLow = low[0];
} else {
    barsIn = barsIn + 1;
    priorHigh = sessHigh;
    priorLow = sessLow;
    if (el_gt(high[0], sessHigh)) sessHigh = high[0];
    if (el_lt(low[0], sessLow)) sessLow = low[0];
}
sessTgtUp = priorLow + midpointFraction * (priorHigh - priorLow);
sessTgtDn = priorHigh - midpointFraction * (priorHigh - priorLow);
